 "energies": "Total energies (eV) of a supercell for classical spin configurations (each spin a unit vector). They are generated by the authors' AMaRaNTA spin model (bilinear exchange of limited range plus single-ion anisotropy), fitted by the authors to their noncollinear LSDA+U calculations with spin-orbit coupling (VASP, PAW, U = 2.8 eV and J_H = 0.8 eV on Cr, constrained moments). The model parameters are withheld. Deterministic noise of DFT-like size (standard deviation 0.02 meV per supercell energy) is added: an identical request returns identical energies. Energies contain an arbitrary constant per magnetic site, the same for all supercells of a compound. Magnetic dipole-dipole interactions are not included (as in the DFT).",
